  "sourceActivityToFirstPartyCrosswalk": [
    {
      "source": "4.1: Estimating a Scale Factor",
      "section": "scale-estimate",
      "teacherKey": "Source mathematical behavior: estimate from ratio center-to-image distance / center-to-preimage distance. Edulytiks example A=(1,1),B=(3,1),C=(8,1): AB2 AC7 => k=7/2=3.5, NOT BC/AB5/2."
    },
    {
      "source": "4.2: Dilations on a Grid",
      "section": "two-centers",
      "teacherKey": "Rectangle A(2,9),B(8,9),C(8,5),D(2,5) with P(3,7), k2 -> (1,11),(13,11),(13,3),(1,3). Source described triangle Q(5,7),R(6,5),S(4,4) about T(2,6): k2 images (8,8),(10,4),(6,2); k1/2 images (3.5,6.5),(4,5.5),(3,5). All from ORIGINAL."
    },
    {
      "source": "4.3: Card Sort: Matching Dilations on a Coordinate Grid",
      "section": "card-sort",
      "teacherKey": "Independent first-party six numbered centers/factors and five lettered full image triples, one unmatched requiring drawing. 1=B,2=E,3=D,4=A,5=C,6=UNMATCHED. 6 center(1,2) k1/2 maps K(1,1)->(1,1.5),L(3,1)->(2,1.5),M(1,2)->(1,2). Extended circle original center(4,0) radius4 about O k3/2 -> center(6,0),radius6."
    }
  ],
  "sourcePracticeToFirstPartyCrosswalk": [
    {
      "source": "Problem 1 equal angles but scale2 not congruent",
      "section": "practice",
      "teacherKey": "No: dilation factor2 doubles corresponding sides, so same angles gives similarity not congruence."
    },
    {
      "source": "Problem 2 quadrilateral PQRS different centers k2 and k1/2",
      "section": "practice",
      "teacherKey": "Original P(7,6),Q(5,4),R(9,3),S(11,5): about R k2 ->(5,9),(1,5),(9,3),(13,7); about O(5,1) k1/2 ->(6,3.5),(5,2.5),(7,2),(8,3); about S k1/2 ->(9,5.5),(8,4.5),(10,4),(11,5)."
    },
    {
      "source": "Problem 3 intersecting line vertical/supplementary angles",
      "section": "practice",
      "teacherKey": "Separate nonparallel crossings: vertical pairs 35/35 and27/27, respective adjacent 145 and153. Do not apply alternate interior theorem."
    },
    {
      "source": "Problem 4 sequence of rigid motions polygon-to-polygon",
      "section": "practice",
      "teacherKey": "Original triangle (0,0),(2,0),(0,1); reflection over y-axis then translation(+3,+1) yields (3,1),(1,1),(3,2). Corresponding lengths angles equal."
    },
    {
      "source": "Problem 5 translation then y-axis reflection then translation",
      "section": "practice",
      "teacherKey": "B(-2,-5) down4->(-2,-9) reflect y->(2,-9) up6->(2,-3)."
    }
  ],
